  message: "PR #2354 (stable-id v19, 2026-11-23/24), locals agent: one more thing the hashed Python signature drops. The hashed path still cuts the signature at 60 characters (_format_function_signature; WI-hopiz widened only the DISPLAY signature to 240 to avoid churning ids), and a cut signature falls to the untyped tier. Long `@overload` stubs of one function therefore tie: poetry has 3 pre-split tie groups before and after the PR, all three long-signature @overload pairs (src/poetry/utils/helpers.py _on_rm_error lines 79/86; ArtifactCache.get_cached_archive_for_link 229/239; SitePackages._path_method_wrapper 158/169). ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v19_11232026/locals/measure/py_ties_fixed.txt. This is the mechanism behind this item's third bullet (an @overload sibling re-minted when its twin changes tier). Hashing the full text moves every Python id whose signature exceeds 60 characters: next scheme bump, churn to be measured."  # a16c
